==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|resorbere|lang=la}}, from {{term|re-||again|lang=la}} + {{term|sorbere||to suck in|lang=la}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} to [[absorb]] (something) again
# {{intransitive}} to undergo [[resorption]]
# {{biology|transitive}} to [[dissolve]] something and [[assimilate]] it.  The loss and re-assimilation of a structure of bone, sinew, suture, or other natural or artificial material. IE1: Because of the loss of direct chewing forces from the teeth to the bone of the jaws, the gums of adhesive denture users change shape as the supporting bone is slowly resorbed.  IE2: After the surgery, the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surgical_suture resorbable sutures] could be felt under the skin, but within a week, they were completely gone.
